The probability estimates follow a similar pattern with best around 0.55-0.70, median at 0.30-0.50, and worst at 0.15-0.30. These thresholds feel appropriate for an EMNLP Main submission with this profile.\n\nNow I'm realizing that lower tail384 values actually indicate a sharper transition, so in the best case scenario I want tail384 to be as low as possible. I'll include both the raw tail384 values and the sharpness ratio but make the directionality clear. Let me finalize the YAML structure with these tiers and their assumptions.\n\nWriting YAML structure... Looking at the reviewer expectations and how the three contributions hold up—the exception dominance finding is solid across all model configurations, the information density analysis pinpoints where the diagnostic signal concentrates with that sharp phase transition around 512 tokens, and the two-tier hierarchy shows remarkable consistency across model scales, with the top tier performing near-perfectly regardless of size.\n\nBut the median reviewer sees things differently: tail-384 appears to show a more gradual transition rather than sharp, the budget curves are mostly consistent across models with just a couple outliers, and they're suggesting I soften the language around the phase transition claim. The key tension is whether that transition is truly sharp or more of a gradual shift, and whether the pattern holds uniformly enough to support the current framing. 我在评估论文的接受概率和审稿人反馈预期，同时调整叙事策略——淡化\"相位转变\"的表述，将第二个主张重新定位为信息密度驱动的压缩效益，强调尾部内容的信息量优于头部但梯度平缓而非陡峭，预算曲线从独立发现降级为支持性可视化。为了补偿这个调整，我需要加强关于异常值仅有损失的尺度不变性的论述。\n\n同时，标签仅有损失的分解（梯度稀释26% vs 信息过载74%）成为第二个主张的核心证据，不再依赖预算曲线的形态，并补充跨模型校准和错误分析来增加证据维度。论文仍有2.5个清晰的贡献可冲击主会议，但需要准备备选方案。最坏的情况是预算曲线矩阵在模型间不一致，没有通用的迹长模式，这需要重新框架化整篇论文的角度。\n\n现在看到的问题是，四个模型间的离散度很大（标准差超过5个百分点），没有统一的转换模式——有些模型单调递增，有些在中间长度出现下降，CodeLlama更是在多个长度点异常。跨种子实验暴露了预算曲线对种子的敏感性，这削弱了具体数值的可信度。审稿人可能会认为这些差异证实了模型依赖性而非普遍性，但唯一的锚点是异常仅有的99.83%在四个模型和三个尺度上保持一致，这个发现不受影响。\n\n现在我在评估各项指标的范围和强度：尾部性能的跨模型不一致性很明显，相位转换的锐度在模型间差异大，只有一到两个模型的预算曲线保持一致，而完整强度的声明也只有一个能维持。这样的结果可能影响在EMNLP主会的接受概率。关键是需要重新框架化论述，但不降低目标期刊的水准——新的角度应该是把异常事件作为唯一能在各模型间实现一致的故障检测信号。\n\n为此，我要彻底放弃预算曲线作为主要贡献，改为在附录中作为完整性报告。论文的核心应该转向三个方向：首先强调异常主导性的普遍性，通过四个模型、三个系列、两个规模和多次种子实验证明异常检测是唯一在所有条件下都稳健的成分；其次精简梯度稀释与信息过载的分解，用标签损失的单一实验就足以支撑；最后保留两层级结构但降为次要贡献。\n\n同时补充零样本/少样本与监督微调的对比来展示实际意义，将论文重新定位为首次系统性的判决预测成分研究，发现最小诊断信号的普遍充分性和尺度不变性。这样以经验严谨性和简洁性胜出的发现来竞争EMNLP主会，而不是依赖设计原理的新颖性。对于顶级会议的强经验研究，50-65%的接受概率是合理的，考虑到数据完整、故事清晰，可能会更高。\n\n现在检查tail384指标的排序逻辑：最优情况下数值较低表示过渡尖锐，中等情况下数值中等表示过渡平缓，最差情况下数值范围宽泛表示不一致，这个对应关系是成立的。\n\n但我意识到最差情况的下界（78）与最优情况的上界（81）重叠了，这违反了排序约束——问题在于最差情况下的均值可能很低（如果某些模型表现尖锐），但关键是跨模型的方差很高。我需要重新定义指标，用跨模型标准差而不是均值来衡量最差情况。\n\n现在我在梳理要包含的指标，确保它们都有一致的排序方向：相位转变锐度、模型一致性、全强度声明和EMNLP接受概率都应该遵循\"最优≥中位≥最差\"的模式。\n\n我还在考虑是否加入tail384的范围数据来帮助实验规划，尽管这些值的排序方向相反（更低=更有利）。现在我需要验证最坏情况下的声明强度值，特别是关于预算曲线混乱时信息密度声明的有效性。\n\n我已经有了异常主导性和两层级结构的完整证据，但声明2更容易受到预算曲线结果的影响，所以我应该将最坏情况下的claims_at_full_strength改为[2, 2]，只有声明1和3能完全成立。\n\n不过声明2虽然被削弱了，但label_only实验仍然支持它——只是失去了预算曲线的佐证，所以它变成了单点证据而非多点曲线。让我更精确地区分：最好情况下3个声明都能完全成立，中位情况下声明2需要软化措辞，最坏情况下声明2需要更大幅度的重构。\n\n实际上，用一个更细致的指标可能更好——我用总贡献强度来评分，从最好的3.0（所有声明完全成立）到中位的2.5（声明1和3完全，声明2部分）再到最坏的2.0（声明1和3完全但声明2显著削弱）。这样能保持一致的排序。\n\n现在让我最后检查一下声明3在最坏情况下是否真的不受影响。两层级结构主要基于Qwen-7B的数据，但跨模型来看，DeepSeek在exception_only模式下的表现在91-99%之间，这取决于种子值。\n\n对比VOTA的84.45%，exception_only明显更好。CodeLlama和Qwen-1.5B也显示相同的趋势，虽然差距较小，但方向一致。所以声明3在所有情况下都应该成立。\n\n现在我需要思考这篇论文的\"最坏情况\"真正意味着什么——既然大部分实验已经完成，核心的...\n\n等等，让我重新整理思路。最坏的情况主要涉及预算曲线可能不够清晰、审稿人对研究范围的批评，以及需要重新表述的问题。但基础部分很扎实——exception_only在4个模型上都达到99.83%，组件消融和校准都很可靠。所以即使是最坏情况也不会很糟糕，主要是表述和次要声明的问题，而不是核心发现本身。这应该反映在我的分层定义中。\n\n我现在有信心写最终输出了。还有一个值得注意的观察：关于\"尾部内容优于头部内容\"这个现象，现有数据已经很清楚地显示了这一点——head-2048大约78-82%，tail-2048大约95-97%。这是一个干净的发现。\n\n我把这个纳入重新表述的叙述中，然后直接输出YAML块，不加任何额外说明。\n\n现在我在整理实验指标，特别是待进行的实验（tail-384）和标签损失的发现。对于label_only_loss，现有数据显示86.22%，相比完整追踪的81.76%提升了4.5个百分点——这个幅度是否足以证明梯度稀释是次要因素取决于预算曲线的支持程度。在不同的论文版本中，这个解释会有所不同：最好的情况下能得出26/74的清晰分解，但如果缺少预算曲线的佐证，审稿人可能会认为单一实验的证据不足。\n\n现在我需要重新检查tail-384的数据范围，特别是Qwen-7B的tail-256结果，因为我看到有两个不同的数值记录。\n\n看起来一个是HEAD截断（前256个token，78.82%），另一个是TAIL截断（最后256个token，77.48%），还有第三个条目显示78.9%，可能是重新运行的结果。为了保持一致性，我会使用这些明确的数值。\n\n现在我在估算Qwen-7B在不同tail截断长度下的性能曲线。从256到512 token之间似乎有显著的性能跳跃，从约78%跃升到93.6%。对于384 token这个中间点，取决于这个转折有多陡峭——如果转折发生在256到384之间，那么384可能已经接近93%；如果转折更陡峭且发生在384到512之间，那么384可能还在78-82%的范围内；如果是平缓过渡，则可能在85-88%之间。现在我需要为其他三个模型（DeepSeek等）估算类似的数据点，以便计算四模型平均值。\n\n从初步数据看，256 token时四模型平均约76.3%，512 token时约95.5%，这意味着384 token的四模型平均可能在77-81%（最乐观情况）到84-89%（中等情况）之间，具体取决于各模型转折点的一致性。\n\n现在我需要调整最坏情况的范围，因为关键问题不是平均值本身，而是模型间的不一致性——我应该用标准差来区分，让最佳情况的标准差最低（0-3%），中等情况稍高（2-5%），最坏情况最高（5-10%），这样即使平均值有重叠，也能通过波动性来区分三种情况。\n\n最终我认为最清晰的方法是以锐度作为主要指标（能够一致地排序：最佳≥中等≥最坏），然后用平均值作为补充参考。\n\n现在我要重新组织这些数值范围，让标准差作为独立指标来衡量一致性，这样就能得到干净的、可预测的排序。\n\nRestructuring the metrics...\n\nActually, I'm realizing I should think about what the reviewer will actually see in the paper—not just the experiment outcomes themselves. The main results table will show exception_only, VOTA, and no_trace accuracies which are stable across all tiers, plus the budget curve which is where the variation happens. The pending experiments around phase transitions and cross-seed robustness are nice additions for completeness but not essential to the core narrative.\n\nLooking at what we already have, the paper's got solid ground: exception dominance is well-characterized across multiple models and seeds, the information density decomposition is clean with the label_only_loss experiment, and the two-tier hierarchy is backed by ablations and calibration work. Even without the phase transition bonus, that's 2.5 strong contributions. The budget curve with our existing 4 points per model already demonstrates the tail-dominance pattern and diminishing returns, so the phase transition finding would just be the cherry on top. The real question is whether the paper needs everything to land perfectly or if it's already competitive—and I think the answer is that we've got a viable paper regardless, with the bonuses determining how exceptional it becomes.\n\nNow I'm looking at the actual numbers from our budget curve experiments to understand what story they're telling.\n\nGenerating markdown table...\n\nThe pattern's clear: tail truncation shows a dramatic improvement jumping from 256 to 512 tokens, then plateaus with minimal gains afterward, though CodeLlama completely breaks down at 2048. Head truncation tells a different story—performance drops significantly when we remove the beginning, suggesting the models rely heavily on initial context. Qwen-7B's full trace baseline gives us a reference point to compare against.\n\nNow I'm working through the YAML structure for the final writeup, and I need to think about how reviewers would likely score this work. For a venue like EMNLP, supportive reviewers would probably land around 3-4 given the solid experimental design with multiple models and seeds, but critics might dock points for the narrow scope of a single task and dataset, pushing them toward 2-3.\n\nGenerating the YAML configuration... Looking at the metrics and confidence ranges for the empirical study — I'm setting bounds on phase transition sharpness, cross-model consistency, and contribution strength, while estimating around 50-65% probability for EMNLP main conference acceptance with expected reviewer scores between 3.5-4.0. The narrative stays focused on three core contributions: exception dominance across multiple seeds as the most robust signal, information density paired with the phase transition phenomenon, and the decomposition of label-only effects.\n\nFor the median scenario, the tail-384 measurements suggest a gradual rather than sharp transition across most models, sitting around 83-89% in the middle of the 256-512 range, so I'm reframing Claim 2 away from sharp phase transition language toward diminishing returns instead. The budget curves show consistent trends across the four models but lack a clear boundary, which supports this more conservative interpretation. 单调递增或仅 2048 退化）但不存在明确拐点\"\n      - \"cross-seed variance 适中（σ 1-3pp at tail-512），noise 不否定趋势但削弱 point estimates 信心\"\n      - \"审稿人对 single-task scope 有保留但接受 empirical depth argument\"\n      - \"label_only_loss 26/74 分解作为 Claim 2 核心证据仍 clean\"\n    number_ranges:\n      phase_transition_sharpness: [0.35, 0.65]\n      budget_curve_consistent_models: [2, 3]\n      tail384_cross_model_std_pp: [2.0, 5.0]\n      contribution_strength: [2.5, 2.5]  # Claims 1+3 全强度,\n      emnlp_main_probability: [0.30, 0.45]\n      expected_reviewer_avg: [3.0, 3.5]\n\n现在我需要调整 Claim 2 的叙述框架：从强调 phase transition 转向突出信息密度在 trace 尾部集中的现象，将 budget curve 降级为辅助图表，同时用 tail-512 相比 head-2048 的 15 个百分点差异（94% vs 79%）来强化信息局部性的论证，并补充 exception_only 的尺度不变性作为额外支撑。\n\n为了增加证据维度，我还需要执行跨模型校准和错误分析。不过最坏的情况是 budget curve 在不同模型间表现出分裂模式——有的单调、有的非单调、CodeLlama 甚至出现多点崩溃——这会削弱 budget curve 作为贡献的有效性，迫使论文重新定位角度。\n\nI'm adjusting the narrative for Claim 2 to emphasize information density concentration in the trace tail rather than phase transitions, demoting the budget curve to a supporting figure while leveraging the 15 percentage point gap between tail and head performance as evidence for information locality. I'm also elevating the exception_only scale invariance finding and planning cross-model calibration and error analysis to strengthen the evidence base. The main risk is that budget curve patterns diverge across models—some monotonic, others non-monotonic, with CodeLlama showing collapse points—which would undermine it as a standalone contribution and require reframing the paper's angle. Looking at the probability ranges and expected reviewer scores, the paper's acceptance prospects are quite limited. The key strategic move is to completely reframe the narrative around exception events as the sole universally robust signal across all model configurations and scales, while demoting the budget curve analysis to supplementary material rather than a core claim. This repositioning elevates the one finding that actually holds up under scrutiny—the consistency of exception-only performance—into the paper's central contribution, though this narrower framing will likely still face resistance from reviewers demanding broader generalization.\n\nFor Claim 2, I'm stripping it down to a single focused experiment showing that gradient dilution is negligible while information overload dominates the performance gap, sidestepping the budget curve entirely. The supporting contributions—the two-tier hierarchy, calibration analysis, and the zero-shot versus fine-tuning comparison—become evidence of analytical rigor rather than novel methodology. The irreducible error analysis and data duplication patterns add methodological depth, positioning the paper as an empirical discovery about unexpected simplicity rather than a principled design innovation, which is the only angle that might compete at EMNLP Main.\n\nNow I'm running through the consistency checks on the key metrics—verifying that transition sharpness, budget curve model counts, cross-model variance, and contribution strength all maintain the expected ordering across best, median, and worst scenarios. I'm verifying that the worst-case scenario still targets EMNLP Main as intended, even though Findings serves as a fallback—the user's \"不降级目标\" (don't downgrade the target) means we shouldn't abandon Main, and that's what the reframing strategy does. I should also make the key_assumptions section more actionable by explicitly mapping which assumptions succeed or fail to each tier, so the user can directly match their actual results to the right scenario.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":53085,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":18,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b2f9c702-d51c-4d47-828